Albrecht Entrati	interacts with	On your first day of service, you aspired to be worthy of me. I only wish that I could have been worthy of you, my Loid.
Albrecht Entrati	interacts with	Loid... You gave me back my sight, but I would not spare you a glance. You gave me back my voice, but I never spoke to praise you as I should have. For you were my right hand. My strength, my support, my sanctuary. Even when the galleries hurled scorn upon me, your sole desire was to suffer it in my stead.
Albrecht Entrati	interacts with	Tenno - I. Require. Your. Trust. Craft the little curio whose blueprints you will find in the computer's memory. Complete the Kalymos Sequence. Repair. Rebuild. When the time is right, find me.
Albrecht Entrati	interacts with	If I had remained in the Deimos laboratory, Loid would never have been safe from ... Him. You know of what I speak. And so I retreated to the only place in history where that entity could not easily follow. To draw His greedy eye away from Loid.
Albrecht Entrati	interacts with	Arthur? Tenno? Forgive me. I need Loid to understand why I had to leave. Without him. Why I forced him to destroy the device after I had gone. And why I could never say the words he so needed to hear.
TV Announcer	interacts with	It's comin' up to midnight, folks! Is YOUR PC ready for the new millennium? Orrrr... are YOU one of the switched-on thinkers who can tell this so-called Y2K event is just a bunch of bullpucky? Stay tuned. Here's where we find out!
Arthur	interacts with	Aoi? Feels like there's... someone in my head...
Aoi	interacts with	They've found me. Keep going, Arthur. Find Dr Entrati. Follow him into hell if you have to! *uses Polarize* (Screaming)
Aoi	interacts with	(breathing heavily) Nearly done with this bitch of a year. I wish we could just start over. Find that Dr. Entrati bastard on day one. Then I wouldn't be alone on New Year's Eve.
Aoi	interacts with	(breathing heavily) Arthur. Find a terminal. Check-in. I need to know you made it.
Bird 3	interacts with	Okay!
Bird 3	interacts with	Talk?" (gasps) "Talk! I can talk! Hey! Hey! Ooh! Ooh! Mister Loid! Mister Loid! Where is Papa? Why did Papa leave us? Mister Loid?
Bird 3	interacts with	MIG? MIG? RE-UN?
Bird 3	interacts with	Zek? Aba! Zek? Zek?
Tagfer	interacts with	Papa is gone. We could all be gone too. In an instant. Like... like... We have to keep quiet.
Tagfer	interacts with	Mara lohk! Mara lohk!
Tagfer	interacts with	IIRE! SHOGRUN UKUL!
Tagfer	interacts with	ZEK! ZEK! ABA? ZEK! ZEK! ABA?
Tagfer	interacts with	(moan)
Fibonacci	interacts with	The strand of Khra has been cut while the Indifference remains undeterred. I foresee a grim and continuing struggle to safeguard Papa's laboratory from its fell and ruinous grasp.
Fibonacci	interacts with	Tenno, the Grimoire must speak with its own voice!
Fibonacci	interacts with	Rrrr. *groan* The strand holds. The Indifference approaches! Soon... it will take on mass.
Fibonacci	interacts with	The sodding Indifference seeks a path through the walls, and then, Tenno, through you! Keep it at bay!
Fibonacci	interacts with	A fell hand raps, uh, upon the Untime Door, and sans Grimoire we are undone! We've been rumbled.
Fibonacci	interacts with	Bravo. It was a long walk toward competence, but here you are. Now, please, the page.
Fibonacci	interacts with	Arousing as I'm sure this is for you, the rest of us are moments away from an extinction Grim! Black! And FINAL! *sigh* So. If you would be so kind. Finish up. So I can point you. Toward. That. Sodding. PAGE!
Fibonacci	interacts with	Papa's daughter excelled at explaining complicated concepts in childish terms. I see now where she learned it.
Fibonacci	interacts with	So long as the Indifference is missing a digit, it is confined to the strands of Khra. Don't ask, your tiny mind would likely pop under the strain of understanding. This limitation is our one hope
Fibonacci	interacts with	Allow me to boil this down for you: should the Indifference's corrupting touch reach us and take back our speech? We would be screwed! So: be a love and eradicate the Murmur in this patch before the big bad gets word that Loid's awake and the fish is talking.
Fibonacci	interacts with	Tenno: the Grimoire is incomplete, the final page hidden away. By Loid. Eh, be a darling and retrieve it. That's all. Run along.
Fibonacci	interacts with	Indeed we have - come, Loid, it's named after Papa's favored pet! Spared the rod and spoiled. We know the Fragmented Ones are heralds of the Indifference. We know the Chosen Operator must summon and destroy them. And regrettably, you, Loid, have made this impossible.
Fibonacci	interacts with	So here we are then: the best of what's left. Clearly Papa's plan was countered. Color me surprised. Right, then. We may proceed with the Sequence.
Fibonacci	interacts with	Here! In the jar!" "Wha? The fish with the big brain?" "YES THE FISH WITH THE BIG BRAIN! Can we PLEASE, finally, get this INTERMINABLE process over with?
Fibonacci	interacts with	YARA MIG! URU URU YARA MIG!
Fibonacci	interacts with	KOMEK! UTEH KOMEK!
Fibonacci	interacts with	YARA MIG! URU URU YARA MIG!
Fibonacci	interacts with	Yara mig!
Loid (Original)	interacts with	...how do I still deserve your tears after all I have done?
Loid (Original)	interacts with	...my last sight of your face must not be marred by tears.
Loid (Original)	interacts with	...do not let it see you weeping, Loid.
Loid (Original)	interacts with	He said...
Loid (Original)	interacts with	'Protect the Vessels. Repair. Rebuild.' So runs the Kalymos Sequence, and such is our task. In the version of the past we saw, My Albrecht said we were too late. The solution, naturally, is to arrive on time, next time. You keep the Murmur at bay, I shall fulfill my role: Punctuality. The Entrati family never could arrive on time without my help. And so... here I am, back to my old role. The diligent servant. Albrecht would have smiled at that, I think.
Loid (Original)	interacts with	Indeed. I shall not waver.
Loid (Original)	interacts with	This stillness... Tenno... No. Operator.
Loid (Original)	interacts with	Get out! There is nothing for you here! Get out! OUT!!
Loid (Original)	interacts with	It takes and it takes! It took my future, it's taking the Labs inch by inch... well, I won't let it take his BLOODY Cavia!
Loid (Original)	interacts with	Tenno? Are you there?! Thank Void! Listen. The Murmur diverted your Extraction-jump. We need you back at the Sanctum, now! Hurry!
Loid (Original)	interacts with	Tenno...
Loid (Original)	interacts with	There. It's done. Keep it to yourself, Tenno. I'm damned if I'm giving Albrecht the last word.
Loid (Original)	interacts with	Do not patronize the Tenno, fish. The strands of Khra are merely Void-renderings of the chains of cause and effect. Conceptually embodied timelines, if you will.
Loid (Original)	interacts with	Tenno... there is some truth to what the... fish... says. That page was the last thing my Albrecht ever wrote. Meant for me. Since I had no interest in reading his endless self-justifications, I hid it away instead. But with all this chaos, it's undetectable.
Loid (Original)	interacts with	So be it - the gift of decency was clearly not bestowed upon the Cavia, Tenno, but I cannot deny the page's current status is lost.
Loid (Original)	interacts with	Choose your words carefully, fish.
Loid (Original)	interacts with	You animals have observed us all this time, have you not? You've given yourself a ROLE in the Sequence?
Loid (Original)	interacts with	Albrecht used you to give the Cavia a voice, just as he used me to keep them alive. Such a resourceful man.
Loid (Original)	interacts with	Where did that come from? Identify yourself!
Loid (Original)	interacts with	Albrecht may have told you to build that thing, but given how he used people and threw them away, he may not have cared for your safety. If that gargoyle is a threat you must take it from the Sanctum immediately. Now, activate it.
Loid (Original)	interacts with	The Jahu Gargoyle. Bring it back here and we shall... examine what 'Form' will do to help us.
Loid (Original)	interacts with	The skin of a martyr doesn't suit you, Albrecht. If something mattered... he'd have found a way. It's too late. You heard him, Tenno! He requires your trust. So craft the bloody thing.
Loid (Original)	interacts with	Would you do the honors?
Loid (Original)	interacts with	Thank you. A moment, please.
Loid (Original)	interacts with	Excellent. Return to me with the board, Tenno.
Loid (Original)	interacts with	Cold stone. Sardonic aloofness. I was a fool not to see the resemblance before.
Loid (Original)	interacts with	Necramites! The lab's automated systems are trying to lock down the Netracell. Your only option is to destroy them.
Loid (Original)	interacts with	The Netracell's security apparatus is diligent. That door won't open while it can sense The Murmur nearby. So. Eliminate them.
Loid (Original)	interacts with	There. A Netracell. Albrecht stored all manner of sentimental old junk in these. Insert the Keyglyph.
Loid (Original)	interacts with	My apologies, Tenno. I shall refrain from further outbursts.
Loid (Original)	interacts with	You are his demon! Not mine! I WON'T listen!
Loid (Original)	interacts with	Keyglyphs are a heavy burden for living beings to bear. Each type will impede you in its own way.
Loid (Original)	interacts with	A Keyglyph. So. The Cavia have provided the very item we require. Very well: proceed to the Netracell at your own risk, Tenno. That babbling oddity may be sending you into a trap, and if you do end up in one, I'm afraid you are on your own.
Loid (Original)	interacts with	It seems Albrecht said more than we heard. Despite the signal becoming corrupted, his words to you are preserved in the Transference buffer. We should extract them... but for that the Pom-2 requires a replacement 'board', and those are all hidden away in the Netracells. You do understand that accessing a Netracell without a Keyglyph is completely impossible?
Loid (Original)	interacts with	If the Cavia have been babbling our secrets to the Murmur, I shall immolate the lot of them, promise or no promise.
Loid (Original)	interacts with	Dust yourself down, Tenno. We are still alive. Rejoin me, and the Kalymos Sequence may proceed.
Loid (Original)	interacts with	I saw off Granum's thugs. I beat back the Infested. And by the Void, I shall see the end of these monstrosities.
Loid (Original)	interacts with	Albrecht once thought the Cavia should have been destroyed. Failures, all. But he briefly showed reluctance, and I saw no reason to punish them for his negligence.
Loid (Original)	interacts with	They're shifting focus! Get to the Vitreum! Look at them. 'The Indifference.' He could have given lessons in indifference.
Loid (Original)	interacts with	There is a defense system, of sorts. Gather enough of the floating Vosphene Glyphs, and they should reinvigorate the organs you're here to protect. A fallback system, in case... the promised Operator never showed.
Loid (Original)	interacts with	The Necramechs could never be compelled to attack the Murmur. Albrecht suspected they could no longer distinguish between the Indifference... and himself. A theory he was reluctant to confirm.
Loid (Original)	interacts with	Here they come. After all those years of creeping, silent encroachment... something has changed them. Stirred them up.
Loid (Original)	interacts with	Ignore the Cavia, Tenno. If Albrecht ever understood their babble, he never bothered to share that knowledge with me.
Loid (Original)	interacts with	The Murmur presumes to destroy our auditory and visual sensors. In all the time I have been asleep, they have never ONCE been so bold!
Loid (Original)	interacts with	Construct - I'm awake. Your one responsibility is fulfilled. Be with the family. They must be kept at the state of ignorance to which my Albrecht so wisely consigned them.
Loid (Original)	interacts with	The Murmur. They're attacking the sensory network I installed, our eyes and ears! To arms, Tenno - play the warrior, and leave the tactics to me!
Loid (Original)	interacts with	SILENCE, CREATURES! It seems the Murmur overloaded your connection. Unfortunately for Albrecht's cherished Pom-2. Not as 'future proof' as the label claimed, alas.
Loid (Original)	interacts with	So... Albrecht made it to 1999 in one piece. But that thing is still on his heels. Albrecht rarely smiled, after his return from the Void. And never like that... I smashed the casket for NOTHING! IT FOLLOWED HIM ANYWAY!
Loid (Original)	interacts with	This isn't right. The Transference stream... it's being diverted!
Loid (Original)	interacts with	Albrecht left a great deal... incomplete. The Vessels are unfinished, like a book one might one day return to. Operable, barely. The Sequence dictates I am to wait for their Operator... Clearly, that cannot be you?
Loid (Original)	interacts with	A Tenno? A deserter, presumably? Is it not aware there's a war going on? *sigh* So. The war, too, is just a memory now.
Loid (Original)	interacts with	Please, follow me, uh...
Loid (Original)	interacts with	Resume your duties, construct.
Loid (Original)	interacts with	Ah. The 'helpful' Necraloid my Albrecht had made, so that I might have assistance... and company. Perhaps that made it... easier for him to leave.
